Loom: a result -> rhs packed-b16 fragment repack reads only bytes 0..1 of each source register (the lane exchange
and the final V_PERM_B32 selectors). When the source fragment is built by vector.from_elements, take lane 2 i's
register for register i directly instead of the packed pair, so the pair packing (one V_PERM_B32 per register with
the zero or don't-care upper lane) is dead and removed. gen_gdn_ss: 8 fewer VALU per repacked tile, row loop
1128 -> 1017 VALU, bit-identical.
